SPRINT — this week

File: openOODA/SPRINT.oot
What to do next. DESIGN is the want. SHIPPED is what exists. PM is the pin.

Handoff
  Read RULES.oot. Then SHIPPED.oot and PM.oot.
  Proof is `oodac check oodac/main.oo` or emit + gcc + run.
  Rebuild from ooda/:
    bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build oodac/main.oo oodac/oodac

Pin
  Release v0.199.0-alpha (Heading to v0.200.0-beta)
  Live check (this machine): OK in about 25 seconds, about 0.32 GiB RAM.
  Rebuild: bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build

Open (Road to Beta — Master Architecture Tracks)

  Track 1: Compiler & Code Generation Floor
  [ ] RTB-6: Pure .wasm binary bytecode emission (upgrade from .wat text to \0asm direct module).
  [ ] RTB-7: Self-host compiler check performance (<10s check & memory optimization under 250MiB).
  [ ] RTB-8: LLVM self-hosting expansion (struct matching & multi-module clang link parity).

  Track 2: Security, Sandboxing & OS Containment
  [ ] RTB-9: Linux Kernel Landlock sandboxing (filesystem path jails under &FsCap).
  [ ] RTB-10: POSIX heap rlimits & memory quotas (hard address-space ceilings under &MemCap).
  [ ] RTB-11: Fine-grained struct field secret taint tracking (allow clean fields, reject secret sinks).

  Track 3: Developer Ecosystem & Tooling Floor
  [ ] RTB-12: Pure self-hosted language server (ooda lsp native JSON-RPC binary replacing JS bridge).
  [ ] RTB-13: Multi-error in-place code fixer (ooda fix auto-patching E_CAP, missing imports & types).
  [ ] RTB-14: Package registry & cryptographic lockfile resolver (pm install/add with SHA-256 seals).

  Track 4: Standard Library Expansion
  [ ] RTB-15: Buffered filesystem stream API (std/fs/file.oo & std/fs/path.oo chunked I/O).
  [ ] RTB-16: Cryptographic hashing & encoding (std/crypto/sha256.oo & std/encoding/base64.oo).
  [ ] RTB-17: Text processing & regular expressions (std/text/regex.oo finite-state engine).

  Track 5: Type System & Formal Verification Depth
  [ ] RTB-18: SMT-backed contract verification (compile-time constraint solving on requires/ensures).
  [ ] RTB-19: Affine & linear typestate lifecycles (compile-time state transitions, no double-free).
  [ ] RTB-20: Zero-cost generics & trait monomorphization (parametric Result[T, E] & List[T] codegen).

  Track 6: Memory Architecture & Hardware-Aware Runtime Depth
  [ ] RTB-21: Scoped arena memory allocators (&ArenaCap high-throughput pointer-bump region reset).
  [ ] RTB-22: Cache-optimized Struct-of-Arrays (SoA / DoD) layout transformation for SIMD vectorization.
  [ ] RTB-23: Deterministic micro-transactional Undo-RAM (ring-buffer memory journal with instant rollback).

  Track 7: Concurrency, Actors & Fault-Tolerant Supervision
  [ ] RTB-24: Location-transparent actor mailboxes & micro-fibers (lockless green-fiber scheduler).
  [ ] RTB-25: Erlang-style OTP supervision trees (hierarchical actor restart, backoff & state recovery).
  [ ] RTB-26: Token-sealed capability RPC (cryptographically authenticated actor wire protocol under &NetCap).

  Track 8: Zero-Trust Security & OS-Kernel Attenuation
  [ ] RTB-27: Hierarchical capability attenuation (scoped sub-capability derivation without ambient leak).
  [ ] RTB-28: Cryptographic object capabilities (C-Caps with HMAC-SHA256 tamper-proof seals).
  [ ] RTB-29: Hardware enclave & confidential compute integration (AMD SEV / Intel SGX for SECRET fields).

  Track 9: Native Code Generation, Binary Tooling & Optimizations
  [ ] RTB-30: Standalone native x86_64 / AArch64 machine-code backend (sub-millisecond compilation).
  [ ] RTB-31: Cross-language link-time optimization (LTO) & direct C-header FFI under &SysCap.
  [ ] RTB-32: Bit-identical reproducible build normalizer (zero-timestamp deterministic binary output).

Later (do not start yet)
